menu "Ping-pong range"

    config PP_BUZZER_GPIO
        int "GPIO the piezo buzzer is on"
        default 1
        range 0 48
        help
            GPIO 1 is pad D0 on the XIAO ESP32S3. The piezo goes between this
            pin and GND.

    config PP_SELF_MM
        int "Distance from the buzzer to the microphone on a board (mm)"
        default 40
        range 0 500
        help
            Each board hears its own sweep a few centimetres away, and the
            result is corrected for it. An error here adds straight onto
            every distance. Measure it, and keep it the same on both boards.

    config PP_TEMP_C10
        int "Air temperature in tenths of a degree C"
        default 200
        range -200 500
        help
            Speed of sound is 331.3 + 0.606 * T m/s: 0.17% per degree.

    config PP_SWEEP_F0
        int "Sweep start (Hz)"
        default 2000

    config PP_SWEEP_F1
        int "Sweep end (Hz)"
        default 6000

    config PP_SWEEP_MS
        int "Sweep length (ms)"
        default 64
        range 20 64

    config PP_DETECT_DB
        int "A sweep must stand this far above the background (dB)"
        default 10
        range 8 30

    config PP_ROUND_MS
        int "Time between ping-pong rounds (ms)"
        default 1500
        range 800 60000

    config PP_REPLY_MS
        int "How long the replying board waits before its sweep (ms)"
        default 500
        range 400 2000
        help
            The detector is deaf for about a third of a second after a sweep,
            so this must stay above 400. A shorter wait leaves less time for
            the two clocks to drift apart between the sweeps.

    config PP_CHANNEL
        int "ESP-NOW channel (both boards must match)"
        default 1
        range 1 13
        help
            The boards leave their Wi-Fi network and sit on this channel.

    config PP_GROUP
        int "Group id: boards only talk to boards with the same id"
        default 1
        range 0 255

    config PP_BUZZER_GPIO2
        int "Second buzzer GPIO for bridge drive (-1: none)"
        default 2
        range -1 48
        help
            With a pin here the buzzer is driven from both pins in opposite
            phase, which doubles the voltage across a piezo: about 6 dB louder.
            GPIO 2 is pad D1 on the XIAO ESP32S3. Wire the piezo between D0
            and D1, NOT to GND. Set -1 to go back to D0 and GND.

    config PP_SELFTEST_S
        int "Buzzer test at boot: seconds of sweeps before ranging starts (0: off)"
        default 30
        range 0 120
        help
            The board plays back-to-back sweeps so the buzzer can be heard and
            its wires checked. Ranging starts when it ends.

endmenu
